mucalc
------------------------------------------
mucalc is a convenient calculator for the command line. It evaluates
mathematical expressions that are given as arguments, read from an input
stream, or typed interactively. In interactive mode, it provides line editing
with tab-completion and persistent history using GNU readline. The evaluation
of expressions is handled by the muParser math parser library.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libmuparser2-2.2.5-1
  libreadline8-8.3-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libmuparser-devel-2.2.5-1
  libreadline-devel-8.3-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://marlam.de/mucalc/

Canonical download:
  https://marlam.de/mucalc/releases/mucalc-2.2.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack mucalc-2.2-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./mucalc-2.2-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/mucalc-2.2-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/mucalc-2.2-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(mucalc)
  /usr/bin/mucalc.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/mucalc.README
  /usr/share/doc/mucalc/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/mucalc/README.md

